{
  "name": "Oldenborn (Ember-Touched): Phoenix Oath",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/BBTTCC_button_icon_phoenix.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Normalized Ancestry Feat.</strong> Formerly granted automatically by <em>Oldenborn (Ember-Touched)</em> at level 17; now available as an optional ancestry feat.</p><p><em>“If you die, you will be furious about it.”</em></p>\n        <p><strong>Phoenix Oath (1/Long Rest).</strong> When you would drop to 0 hit points, you instead drop to 1 hit point and erupt in a controlled blaze. Each hostile creature within 10 feet takes fire damage equal to 2d6 + your proficiency bonus, and you immediately end one condition affecting you (charmed, frightened, or restrained).</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"phoenixOath\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #c08e6a;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(95,65,45,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e8b890;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Phoenix Oath</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/long rest &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Reaction (auto, on dropping to 0 HP) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">When you would drop to 0 HP, instead drop to 1 HP and erupt — hostile creatures within 10 ft take 2d6+PB fire, end one condition (charmed/frightened/restrained).</div>\n</div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
